[Ultracache](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache#ultracache) requires Nx 24.0.0 or later.
Once [Ultracache is on](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache#turn-on-ultracache) for your workspace in Nx Cloud, Nx 24 and later use it in CI by default.
Runs outside CI always hash tasks from the `inputs` declared in your project configuration.

Earlier Nx versions don't support Ultracache.
To use it, [update your workspace](/docs/features/automate-updating-dependencies) to Nx 24.0.0 or later.

## Control Ultracache for one pipeline

Set `NX_CLOUD_ULTRACACHE_MODE` in a CI pipeline to override the workspace setting for that pipeline only.
Set it to `on` to try Ultracache on one branch before you turn it on for the workspace, or to `off` to skip it for one pipeline.
For every value and where to set it, see [try Ultracache on one branch or workflow](/docs/features/ci-features/remote-cache#try-ultracache-on-one-branch-or-workflow).

To turn Ultracache off for a single target instead, set [`ultracache.mode`](/docs/reference/project-configuration#ultracache) to `off`.

## When Nx can't read the recordings

Nx makes one attempt to read the recordings from Nx Cloud.
If the read fails, the run continues and Nx hashes every task in that run from its declared `inputs`.
